@startuml raditrack_data_flow
!theme plain
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 250
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

title RADiTrack — Data Flow & TAT Calculation (Zero-PII)

actor "Administrator\n(prototype data entry)" as Admin
actor "Radiologist /\nResident" as Doctor
participant "RIS Simulator /\nImport exams\n(staff dashboard)" as Intake
participant "RADiTrack\nserver actions" as Server
database "Supabase\nPostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Staff dashboard\n(other open tabs)" as StaffUI
participant "Patient TV\n(/patient)" as PublicUI

note over Admin, Intake
  Until the hospital approves RIS access, exams enter through the RIS Simulator
  or a spreadsheet import. The planned RIS Sync Agent would add exams the same way,
  reading the read-only view raditrack.vw_exams every 5 minutes.
end note

' ==============================================================================
== 1. Examination completed (enters the backlog) ==
' ==============================================================================

Admin -> Intake: Log completed exam\n(accession no., modality, patient category)\nor upload an .xlsx / .csv file
Intake -> Server: createExaminationAction (T1 = time logged)\nor import: previewExamImportAction, then commitExamImportAction
activate Server
Server -> Server: Import only: validate every row\n(known modality & category, times in order,\nnot in the future, accession not already used)
Server -> DB: INSERT examinations\n(status EXAM_COMPLETED, exam_completed_at = T1;\nimported signed exams also get their report)
DB --> Server: Saved
Server --> Intake: Done
deactivate Server
Intake -> StaffUI: BroadcastChannel "DB_CHANGED"\n(other tabs refresh at once)
PublicUI -> Server: Refresh every 10 s:\ngetPublicActivityData
Server -> DB: Count today's exams by modality\nand category (Manila date)
DB --> Server: Counts only
Server --> PublicUI: Today's counts (no patient details)

' ==============================================================================
== 2. Report signed off (TAT and SLA breach calculated) ==
' ==============================================================================

Doctor -> StaffUI: Examinations → Backlog → Sign off
StaffUI -> Server: signOffReportAction(examId)
activate Server
Server -> DB: Read exam + SLA targets for its modality
DB --> Server: exam_completed_at (T1), targets
Server -> Server: T2 = now\nTAT = T2 − T1 (minutes)\nbreach = TAT > target for the exam's\nmodality + patient category
Server -> DB: In one transaction:\nUPSERT radiology_reports (report_signed_at = T2,\ntat_exam_to_sign_minutes, is_sla_breached)\nUPDATE examinations (status COMPLETED_SIGNED_OFF)
DB --> Server: Saved
Server --> StaffUI: Done (page revalidated)
deactivate Server

' ==============================================================================
== 3. Dashboard and report read the figures ==
' ==============================================================================

Doctor -> StaffUI: Choose time window,\nmodality, patient category
StaffUI -> Server: fetchFilteredExecutiveKpiAction,\nfetchModalityTatDataAction,\nfetchSevenDayAnalyticsAction,\nfetchYearlyTrendAction
Server -> DB: Query exams and reports in the window
DB --> Server: Rows
Server -> Server: Count, average and median TAT,\nSLA %, backlog, prior-period change
Server --> StaffUI: KPI cards, TAT by modality,\n7-day table, 12-month trend
note right of StaffUI
  The PDF report (/report) calls the same
  functions, so its numbers match the screen.
end note

@enduml
